desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Current Exe"
	title_zh: "Current Exe"
	type: vuln
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-current-exe"
	risk: "information-exposure"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `current-exe` (rust/lang/security/current-exe.yml).
Original message: current_exe should not be used for security operations. From the docs: "The output of this function should not be trusted for anything that might have security implications. Basically, if users can run the executable, they can change the output arbitrarily."
CWE: CWE-807: Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision
References:
- https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/env/fn.current_exe.html#security
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rs": <<<POS
std::env::current_exe()
POS
	"safefile://pos.rs": <<<NEG
std::env::current_dir()
NEG
)

${*.rs}.pattern_regex(/(?:std::env::current_exe\(\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "Current Exe",
	title_zh: "Current Exe",
	message: "Current Exe detected.",
}
